# Normalize line endings: everything text is committed with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
# The Windows batch script must keep CRLF to run under cmd.exe.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# PowerShell is more forgiving than cmd.exe, but these scripts GENERATE
# batch files, and a batch file with LF endings breaks under cmd.exe -
# which cost a day of diagnosis when a generated runvim.cmd inherited
# LF from a here-string in an LF-committed .ps1.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Registry Editor is more forgiving about line endings than cmd.exe's
# "goto", but a .reg file is Windows-only regardless - keep it CRLF too.
*.reg text eol=crlf
# The recording at the top of README.md is bytes, whatever text=auto's
# heuristic makes of it.
*.gif binary
